OL,3,GNEWSASycamore Gap trees among those
OL,4,Aforming new woodland
OL,5,
OL,6,FPeople are being invited to help plant
OL,7,F169,000 trees - including saplings
OL,8,Fgrown from the Sycamore Gap tree - as
OL,9,Fpart of a new woodland.
OL,11,FNational Trust Wallington, near
OL,12,FMorpeth, Northumberland, is running
OL,13,Fcommunity tree-planting sessions on 21,
OL,14,F24 and 25 November, and said no
OL,15,Fexperience or specialist equipment was
OL,16,Fneeded to join.
OL,18,FThe 109-hectare (269-acre) new woodland
OL,19,Fat Elf Hills would eventually include
OL,20,Fareas managed primarily for nature,
OL,21,Fproductive woodland and open woodland
OL,22,Fpasture, the National Trust said.
OL,23,APub: 18-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
